    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A nomadic people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu-corridor">Gansu corridor</a>, strong enough in the 3rd century BCE to hold the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modu-chanyu">Modu</a> hostage.</li><li>Defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a>, they migrated west to the Ili valley and then took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a>, probably in the 130s BCE.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-qian">Zhang Qian</a>'s mission to them opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han China</a> to the West, and their Guishuang chiefs founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushan-empire">Kushan Empire</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> turned the skull of a defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuezhi">Yuezhi</a> king into a drinking cup; according to the Han shu, Han envoys later drank from it when swearing a blood oath with a Xiongnu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanyu">chanyu</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

